 "summaries": [
  {
   "version": "Introduced in House",
   "date": "2023-06-12",
   "text": "Children Don't Belong on Tobacco Farms Act\nThis bill prohibits an individual under the age of 18 from performing work that has direct contact with tobacco plants or dried tobacco leaves by specifying that the work is oppressive child labor. (Oppressive child labor is generally prohibited under the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938, with some exceptions.)"
  }
